Jarek, Olek,

thank you both, this is much clearer than my own notes. Let me pull it together and then ask three things of you.

Status: the ad for KC-DIS-094 went live on Monday 30 September on our careers page and on two portals (the second one only because Wacek's cousin works there, I am not going to pretend otherwise). It closes on Friday 25 October, which has now passed, and we ended with 33 applications. Of those I screened out 21 on the basis of "no night-shift or 24/7 operations experience at all", which leaves 12, and after the phone screens (I did them on 14 to 18 October, 25 minutes each) the shortlist is five people. Headcount reference for the role is HC-2025-017; it was approved by Priya on 8 October as a 2025 role although we want to start in January.

The shortlist, in the order of the CV pile and not in any order of preference:

1. Marcin Olszewski. Eleven years at a liner agency in Gdańsk, the last four as shift lead. Notice period three months, so earliest start 1 January 2025. Expectation 9,200 PLN gross base. He left me a voicemail on 10 October that was very polite and nearly unintelligible because the transcript called our job ad "the add".
2. Beata Kasprzak. Eight years in rail freight dispatch (PKP-style operations, I will not name the company), shift supervisor for the last two. Notice one month. Expectation 8,800 PLN.
3. Oskar Lindgren. Swedish, currently at a ferry operator in Gothenburg, wants to relocate to Gdynia for family reasons. Speaks Swedish, English and passable Polish. Notice two months. Expectation 9,600 PLN and he wants a relocation package. I have not asked him what he means by a package.
4. Natalia Wójcik. Six years in air cargo handling at Gdańsk airport, no reefer experience but cold chain adjacent (pharma cargo). Notice one month. Expectation 8,600 PLN.
5. Karol Brzeziński. Five years as dispatcher at a road haulier in Tczew, weakest on systems, strongest on temperament, according to the phone screen. Notice two weeks. Expectation 8,300 PLN.

Dates. I proposed Tuesday 5 November for the interviews, but Jarek pointed out that Helvetia audit is that same day at 10:00 and he cannot be in two rooms. New proposal: interviews on Thursday 7 November, five slots of 60 minutes starting at 13:00, in room 12 on the ground floor. The simulation (see below) takes place on the night desk on the following Monday night, 11 November, from 22:00 to 23:30, for the three candidates who pass the interview.

The panel is Jarek, Olek and me. Wacek is cc'd for information only and has asked to be allowed to shake hands with candidates in the corridor. Fine.

Scoring sheet, so we do not argue afterwards: the simulation counts for 40 %, the interview for 30 %, the references for 20 % and "fit with the owls" for 10 %. Olek owns the fit score. The simulation scenario is a dairy alarm with the yard hub offline and no acknowledgment from the contact on file, which Olek designed after the June incident and which he swears is "survivable but only just". Candidates get 90 minutes with a printed guide to the Tidewalk alarm groups and the night desk phone.

Money. I can offer up to 9,000 PLN gross base within the O4 grade without anyone else; above that I need Priya. The night supplement is on top, per the contract template, and is not part of the number we quote. Probation is three months. I would like to offer on Friday 15 November and have the person start on 1 January if their notice allows it, otherwise on 1 February 2025.

Three questions:
(a) Olek, will you be on the desk on the 11th, or should I ask Mateusz to stand in as the "dispatcher on shift"?
(b) Jarek, do you want Priya to see the offer before it goes out? She asked.
(c) Both of you: shall we still use the agency? See below.

Ines

Ines Baptista-Okafor | Head of People & Culture
Korvane Cold Chain Sp. z o.o. | ul. Łużycka 14, 81-537 Gdynia | +48 58 555 0127

